        "title": "Hosted dev-loop harness authentication fixed",
        "summary": "Dev-loop control routes now forward the caller's JWT and per-run harness auth token when reaching hosted harnesses, unblocking swarm runs that previously failed to authenticate.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Pause, stop, resume, and status endpoints for the dev loop now extract the caller's JWT and thread it through control_loop and detached-run lookups, so hosted harness requests are properly authenticated instead of being issued anonymously.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "103f2631ebc56b39284d42e74e3fd80642f63ab5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Each running loop now tracks a per-run harness_auth_token alongside its base URL, letting control actions reuse the exact credential the run was started with when dispatching to the hosted harness.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "103f2631ebc56b39284d42e74e3fd80642f63ab5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Introduced a dedicated harness_transport module and harness_for_base_url helper so local versus hosted harness selection and auth handling live in one place instead of being reimplemented per control action.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "103f2631ebc56b39284d42e74e3fd80642f63ab5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Hosted dev-loop harness now receives auth tokens",
      "Pause, stop, resume, and status propagate the caller JWT",
      "New harness_transport layer centralizes harness calls"
